<section id="energy">
  <h2>Energy</h2>
  <p>Crude closed mixed overnight, Brent at {{ BRENT_LAST }} ({{ BRENT_D1_CHG_USD }}, {{ BRENT_D1_CHG_PCT }}%) and WTI at {{ WTI_LAST }} ({{ WTI_D1_CHG_USD }}, {{ WTI_D1_CHG_PCT }}%); Brent–WTI arb at {{ BRENT_WTI_SPREAD }}. Front of the Brent curve held backwardation (BRENT_1M2M_SPREAD) though Dec/Dec flattened by DEC_DEC_CHG, signaling positioning rather than balances. Brent–Dubai (BRENT_DUBAI_EFS) widened, keeping arbs open for Atlantic barrels East. Refined products lagged — Sing gasoil crack (GASOIL_CRACK_SING) softer alongside gasoline (GASOLINE_CRACK_SING) on weak regional demand.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Flat: Brent {{ BRENT_LAST }}, WTI {{ WTI_LAST }}, NatGas {{ NATGAS_LAST }} ({{ NATGAS_D1_CHG_PCT }}%), Gasoil {{ GASOIL_LAST }} ({{ GASOIL_D1_CHG_PCT }}%), Dubai DUBAI_1M.</li>
    <li>Curves: BRENT_1M2M_SPREAD (back), WTI_1M2M_SPREAD (flattening), DUBAI_M1M3 widening vs Brent.</li>
    <li>Flows: paper hedging from N. Asia refiners; airline jet hedging picked up at JET_SING_CRACK.</li>
    <li>Inventories: API showed CRUDE_API_CHG; DOE tonight at DOE_TIME, consensus DOE_CRUDE_CONSENSUS.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Watch for Asia session</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>{{ BRENT_LAST }} key pivot — break of BRENT_SUPPORT opens BRENT_DOWNSIDE_TARGET; upside capped at BRENT_RESISTANCE.</li>
    <li>Clients look offside long middle distillates; further crack weakness likely triggers stop-outs.</li>
    <li>Catalysts: OPEC+ JMMC commentary, US DOE, headline risk from RED_SEA_STATUS shipping.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

